# Phase C results bloat (added 2026-05-10 PM):
# - .pt checkpoint files: 1+ GB each, 8 ranks × N rounds = tens of GB
# - wandb/ local sync dirs are auto-managed, don't commit
# - per_token .jsonl files can be 100+ MB at long ctx
# - lever_validation/ holds A/B experiment data we don't need in main
# Keep CSVs (small, human-readable) and memory_trace JSONs (small, paper-grade).
results/**/checkpoints/
results/**/wandb/
results/**/per_token/
results/lever_validation/

# MLSys (2026-10-04): results/mlsys/per_token/ IS a committed deliverable —
# it holds the 3-seed per-round traces the Phase 4 dip test consumes, and
# the whole point of the MLSys phase-2 reruns is to get all three seeds
# into one analysis directory. The "100+ MB" concern above does not apply
# here: these files carry one record per ROUND (~200 B), not per token, so
# the committed set measures ~40 KB for 6 traces. results/final/per_token/
# is already tracked under the same reasoning.
!results/mlsys/per_token/

# MLSys run-state: created on the pod and pulled back. Markers are
# per-instance progress flags, meaningless locally, and shipping them
# back to a fresh instance makes stages skip ("already complete").
# Never commit them.
results/mlsys/.markers/
results/m4_smoke/long_smoke.v4_oom.csv
*.pt

# LaTeX build artifacts
manuscript/**/main.aux
manuscript/**/main.blg
manuscript/**/main.bbl
manuscript/**/main.log
manuscript/**/main.out
manuscript/**/main.toc

# arXiv submission build artifacts (regenerable; flattened-path copies)
manuscript/**/arxiv-submission/
manuscript/**/arxiv-submission.tar.gz
